  'This course develops the professional knowledge, judgment, evidence discipline, and ethical stance needed for high-quality audit and assurance work. Students learn audit standards, risk assessment, materiality, internal controls, audit evidence, sampling, transaction-cycle testing, audit reporting, fraud response, analytics, IT audit, and emerging assurance services.',
  $audjson${"slug": "auditing", "title": "Auditing", "description": "This course develops the professional knowledge, judgment, evidence discipline, and ethical stance needed for high-quality audit and assurance work. Students learn audit standards, risk assessment, materiality, internal controls, audit evidence, sampling, transaction-cycle testing, audit reporting, fraud response, analytics, IT audit, and emerging assurance services.", "topics": [{"id": "2bbde5a5-2a30-40a4-a1ef-7b8ff7ebd38c", "type": "topic", "title": "Audit Function, Assurance Services, and the Public-Interest Role", "description": "Students learn why auditing exists, how assurance reduces information risk, and how auditors serve investors, boards, regulators, and society.", "children": [{"id": "a29e3cbd-c0a3-44f8-9fb6-7828a130b80c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purpose of auditing", "children": [{"id": "b4cfccd2-4e59-4a22-937e-6bef9fd37d79", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency theory and information asymmetry"}, {"id": "34188fdb-30c0-4440-9afb-8900ffe1ae7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reasonable assurance versus absolute assurance"}, {"id": "3e840e99-2665-4b13-9c5e-e7fd4c193d3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit value for capital markets and governance"}], "description": "The point is to understand auditing as a trust and information-risk mechanism."}, {"id": "e1a0f67f-2d80-45b1-b67b-3223922fac82", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assurance landscape", "children": [{"id": "6d589bc9-ed85-4b16-80f2-f823bb0c029e", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial statement audits"}, {"id": "22ae6d53-173a-4be6-a1f5-a8b6c674dfe9", "type": "concept", "title": "Reviews, compilations, attestation, agreed-upon procedures, and SOC engagements"}, {"id": "9b44468b-4a39-4cf4-b692-a7e950e0a391", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal audit, external audit, government audit, and forensic work"}], "description": "Students distinguish audits from adjacent services before learning technical procedures."}, {"id": "ed673ee4-18c5-4262-b22f-341125934aec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit profession and public interest", "children": [{"id": "34c1447f-3fbf-4ee2-8ec6-0f40d915852d", "type": "concept", "title": "Investor protection"}, {"id": "63003f1c-d9c5-4f5d-ab7b-410dae9b36f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Board audit committees and governance"}, {"id": "bfadcb7b-c137-435c-9cd5-05d28f1b1cc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit failures, restatements, and public trust"}], "description": "Auditing starts with why audit quality matters."}]}, {"id": "5c91045f-e6b3-49db-a110-5210920f7254", "type": "topic", "title": "Professional Standards, Regulation, Ethics, and Independence", "description": "This module grounds students in PCAOB, AICPA, IAASB, SEC, and professional ethics requirements.", "children": [{"id": "433a449e-b897-42f2-bece-a5c0a0ed6d9c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Standards ecosystem", "children": [{"id": "871c0ce1-d7f3-4e54-ae76-6a82f69d5fa2", "type": "concept", "title": "PCAOB standards for public-company audits"}, {"id": "cc02f52c-32c7-406d-a0da-bd07c787106a", "type": "concept", "title": "AICPA standards for nonissuers"}, {"id": "31740e81-5333-4f5c-b0e3-5fedfc5d65be", "type": "concept", "title": "IAASB international auditing standards"}], "description": "Students learn which standards apply to which engagement and client type."}, {"id": "7b25df0f-6bf9-4c37-bb94-09252e225f31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and independence", "children": [{"id": "634a48b7-fd74-404b-adcf-9da2f7062833", "type": "concept", "title": "Independence in fact and appearance"}, {"id": "193ae094-1568-4e9e-9059-9518caf4d4d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts of interest, confidentiality, and objectivity"}, {"id": "0f6fd4b5-96bf-4c4a-bbc1-19cbffd7ce4d", "type": "concept", "title": "SEC, PCAOB, AICPA, and IESBA ethics concepts"}], "description": "Auditors must be technically competent and visibly independent."}, {"id": "d0175360-ac22-42bc-8a7d-cfee9d4429c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulatory oversight", "children": [{"id": "ca0f2055-5290-4e55-8a23-3e957beac289", "type": "concept", "title": "SEC and PCAOB roles"}, {"id": "f353f31a-f6ea-4e0b-9667-530c76ea023b", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review and firm quality management"}, {"id": "dc6fbf45-e3e0-4f84-b258-d7e8b48a5f77", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection findings and enforcement cases"}], "description": "Students learn how inspection, enforcement, and standard setting shape practice."}]}, {"id": "bd4c5740-6b6c-418d-8a4f-72ca4c749c54", "type": "topic", "title": "Client Acceptance, Engagement Planning, and Audit Strategy", "description": "Students learn how auditors decide whether to accept an engagement and how they translate risk into an audit plan.", "children": [{"id": "39ada265-708c-4ff5-8529-f9206be6f837", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Client acceptance and continuance", "children": [{"id": "069aeea6-181f-41cb-9d62-b8d52010064c", "type": "concept", "title": "Integrity of management"}, {"id": "03120861-fda1-4783-bb6a-814d146fa058", "type": "concept", "title": "Independence and competence"}, {"id": "ae7c2b2d-6f3d-4541-8b49-571b795ce3ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Engagement letters and scope"}], "description": "Auditors begin by deciding whether the engagement risk is acceptable."}, {"id": "316ab5b8-0090-4afe-9abb-b16243efd00f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Understanding the client", "children": [{"id": "8273689b-ed6e-4043-b8e7-4d6d19f1e5d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Business model and industry risks"}, {"id": "ac6906f0-15d4-4546-bf4c-4333781d121c", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance and audit committee communication"}, {"id": "b4c16d4f-aa4e-44f6-9eee-d143f81cc01b", "type": "concept", "title": "Preliminary analytics and financial statement trends"}], "description": "Planning requires a disciplined view of the business, industry, systems, and financial reporting risks."}, {"id": "1a1722e4-f9b6-44ed-847a-a0ed84261a7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit strategy and plan", "children": [{"id": "a2dc81c6-74f2-4b30-9963-d3f5d90563f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Overall audit strategy"}, {"id": "81ea1479-a962-430e-b9fb-eb964524174b", "type": "concept", "title": "Detailed audit plan"}, {"id": "104406ee-e4cd-4ebf-a663-db3e7fe25301", "type": "concept", "title": "Use of specialists, component auditors, and internal audit"}], "description": "Students learn to translate risk into staffing, timing, and testing choices."}]}, {"id": "ccd3b8f4-4534-4784-b5d6-cc5004e523cf", "type": "topic", "title": "Audit Risk Model, Materiality, and Professional Judgment", "description": "This topic develops the judgment framework auditors use to scope work, evaluate misstatements, and respond to risk.", "children": [{"id": "ba837505-4129-4768-93a0-81774b9da312", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit risk model", "children": [{"id": "03383580-eb08-45d5-8578-788048fd065c", "type": "concept", "title": "Inherent risk"}, {"id": "20330c0a-bb57-4d43-8b88-0ab4d79c7801", "type": "concept", "title": "Control risk"}, {"id": "861cfa01-e75b-47d0-b144-e8964e4da0f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Detection risk and planned procedures"}], "description": "The model helps auditors connect inherent, control, detection, and overall audit risk."}, {"id": "dee37ea3-cef1-4ec0-b4b8-7740c835374e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Materiality", "children": [{"id": "b03d7160-170f-4715-9909-aeca94adcd19", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning materiality"}, {"id": "d11ea835-2ccf-4336-85f6-e5d153a4b312", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance materiality"}, {"id": "02df76bd-694d-40c2-911d-9be58d77af55", "type": "concept", "title": "Clearly trivial thresholds"}], "description": "Materiality focuses the audit on misstatements that could influence users."}, {"id": "994c1c1f-eafb-45b4-b1da-732fa033bcb1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional judgment", "children": [{"id": "1366b407-92d5-4df3-9498-16c5e946116b", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk response decisions"}, {"id": "8d66e85d-0550-4e04-8c99-4bf892ddeee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias and judgment traps"}, {"id": "34cf8001-c8cb-4cf0-b274-4b1026ac045f", "type": "concept", "title": "Consultation, supervision, and review"}], "description": "Students learn how auditors reason under uncertainty and document judgment."}]}, {"id": "ab432d3c-c5b0-40aa-9afd-89150bd3e02d", "type": "topic", "title": "Management Assertions, Audit Objectives, and Financial Reporting Foundations", "description": "Students connect audit procedures to assertions, financial statement elements, GAAP, and disclosure risks.", "children": [{"id": "ba6d28a1-b00f-4a51-ad2c-adc52a5193fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assertions", "children": [{"id": "449327dd-d277-4107-a010-ea54da23a830", "type": "concept", "title": "Existence, completeness, valuation, rights and obligations"}, {"id": "c2acf208-75f1-4aa3-83cc-34c13632e708", "type": "concept", "title": "Occurrence, cutoff, accuracy, and classification"}, {"id": "dbb5195c-f8c6-46f5-978d-3a7dfe4b07fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation and disclosure"}], "description": "Assertions provide the bridge between financial statement accounts and audit procedures."}, {"id": "4382c0df-304b-4d99-af86-a904ad85331f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit objectives", "children": [{"id": "568ae74f-92c0-4b3b-a1fd-15bb9367f8fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Transaction objectives"}, {"id": "5fcdf08b-1a2e-4b30-9c7b-c5df2f56b440", "type": "concept", "title": "Balance objectives"}, {"id": "44afda37-bf71-43d1-b6fa-14d9ae0e247d", "type": "concept", "title": "Disclosure objectives"}], "description": "Students learn to write procedures that directly address specific risks."}, {"id": "dd362c80-5461-4139-9bd7-8de5b8f3251d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial reporting foundations", "children": [{"id": "a384f10a-4d50-4654-9ca6-4f298831f3c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue recognition, leases, estimates, and contingencies"}, {"id": "a2b78198-5f8c-4d84-9f8c-a651b7ce4720", "type": "concept", "title": "Fair value, impairment, and financial instruments"}, {"id": "c01d9e6f-478e-410c-ac2e-5decacff4b7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Consolidations, foreign currency, and related parties"}], "description": "Auditors need enough accounting depth to identify high-risk reporting issues."}]}, {"id": "3cba1248-0043-4635-8781-16993d449c17", "type": "topic", "title": "Internal Control, COSO, SOX, and ICFR Audits", "description": "This module covers internal control frameworks, control design, control operation, and integrated audits of financial statements and ICFR.", "children": [{"id": "81ef7de1-b16f-4330-b8ca-8966df96c957", "type": "subtopic", "title": "COSO framework", "children": [{"id": "7607a675-4ebc-4a33-b789-8776771f1a49", "type": "concept", "title": "Control environment"}, {"id": "08670f4b-6451-47e0-a2f5-9fc8ee758924", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment, control activities, information/communication, and monitoring"}, {"id": "ffbf1630-c1f4-4b79-a6b8-b769d9d0deb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Entity-level versus process-level controls"}], "description": "COSO gives auditors a structured language for evaluating control systems."}, {"id": "6ea715cd-ab34-4a7b-aea9-f795ed5141d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "SOX and ICFR", "children": [{"id": "0fee2404-06fc-4efb-8738-3728e7e25de6", "type": "concept", "title": "Management assessment"}, {"id": "adf3827f-cb01-44ac-84b7-97b5f453887c", "type": "concept", "title": "Auditor attestation"}, {"id": "9baa82bd-e294-4c5a-a4ce-930807f6ed20", "type": "concept", "title": "Material weaknesses and significant deficiencies"}], "description": "Public-company audits require integrated thinking about financial statements and internal control."}, {"id": "101dd6b6-f1e6-4006-b63a-818ca5765299", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Control testing", "children": [{"id": "e1755ac5-0ab2-40ca-b544-80a802d7c943", "type": "concept", "title": "Walkthroughs"}, {"id": "1307610d-0f8a-4ffa-aea5-177e9ca6483f", "type": "concept", "title": "Inquiry, observation, inspection, and reperformance"}, {"id": "8d5c0275-65c7-44b9-9b3f-fbccec007f65", "type": "concept", "title": "Control deficiencies and remediation"}], "description": "Students learn to evaluate design and operating effectiveness."}]}, {"id": "0239bae4-7765-48d5-bd1c-91fb14e61b7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Audit Evidence, Documentation, and Workpaper Quality", "description": "Students learn what counts as persuasive evidence and how workpapers support conclusions, supervision, and inspection.", "children": [{"id": "df8d3b13-eb43-459b-9999-7c222f8cd686", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence concepts", "children": [{"id": "358f1380-bc1d-4cac-a14d-75051823125e", "type": "concept", "title": "Relevance and reliability"}, {"id": "af6a1391-df8f-4f55-ad18-47ff28517801", "type": "concept", "title": "Sufficiency and appropriateness"}, {"id": "92130fe7-3622-449c-8042-53e1a16867ce", "type": "concept", "title": "External confirmations and third-party evidence"}], "description": "Auditors gather sufficient appropriate evidence before issuing conclusions."}, {"id": "2a853c01-05d7-4f68-b843-a6be4a9fe8ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation standards", "children": [{"id": "7c4284ed-b873-4251-b7c7-dd3f34b20bc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Purpose, procedure, evidence, conclusion"}, {"id": "289cf1e3-a725-4acf-a577-00f9c66b660e", "type": "concept", "title": "Tick marks, indexing, and cross-references"}, {"id": "4c0eaf29-0f8e-427f-be31-18900c3b5583", "type": "concept", "title": "Retention and confidentiality"}], "description": "Workpapers must tell a clear story for reviewers and inspectors."}, {"id": "f32e3385-ff81-459b-8210-f0694cccc788", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inspection-ready work", "children": [{"id": "b55ade6c-a211-4734-aa5f-eb759e90e2e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear risk linkage"}, {"id": "5aded6b4-30c5-4cf3-953f-dd15b7f7873c", "type": "concept", "title": "Resolution of exceptions"}, {"id": "6b3b5c6b-ee20-4437-9acf-2532f50a4f36", "type": "concept", "title": "Supervision, review notes, and signoffs"}], "description": "Documentation anticipates review questions."}]}, {"id": "34ff917e-0736-48b9-b865-c9b461f399be", "type": "topic", "title": "Substantive Procedures, Analytical Procedures, and Audit Sampling", "description": "This topic develops the procedures used to test account balances, transactions, estimates, and disclosures.", "children": [{"id": "931b1a82-2a89-4c1a-b970-efd22b8e2b97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Substantive testing", "children": [{"id": "15fb9224-3c8e-4c81-91ce-7a25ed01ce4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Tests of details"}, {"id": "3a8e8692-2d58-4e5d-9b61-0beb078b5004", "type": "concept", "title": "Substantive analytical procedures"}, {"id": "81fd36a8-0713-4484-8874-7207431e8207", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutoff, recalculation, confirmation, and inspection"}], "description": "Students learn how auditors test details when controls alone are insufficient."}, {"id": "dd9066a8-a9da-4722-924d-ea64491dc37e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytical procedures", "children": [{"id": "3f33f56d-7948-4462-b28e-ea5c6607f21c", "type": "concept", "title": "Expectation development"}, {"id": "908424ff-8e3b-4219-b914-7a402deaf380", "type": "concept", "title": "Thresholds and investigation"}, {"id": "ff3e6120-5f70-4096-b49f-b6b7e3392563", "type": "concept", "title": "Ratio, trend, regression, and reasonableness testing"}], "description": "Analytics support planning, substantive testing, and final review."}, {"id": "09c0629a-7b68-4e45-84a2-a0c04e288947", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling", "children": [{"id": "6599e0a8-3168-4368-8276-5000355438e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Statistical and nonstatistical sampling"}, {"id": "0efba2bf-250c-45cc-b15d-c9f5fefc5ca2", "type": "concept", "title": "Attribute and variables sampling"}, {"id": "8ffb04d7-6d07-468f-acbd-4e340742d76d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling risk, tolerable misstatement, and projection"}], "description": "Sampling balances audit efficiency with evidence quality."}]}, {"id": "674a2fec-11e5-47c8-b0e0-b352068a16a6", "type": "topic", "title": "Auditing Major Transaction Cycles", "description": "Students apply risk, controls, and evidence concepts to revenue, purchasing, payroll, inventory, cash, financing, and financial reporting cycles.", "children": [{"id": "221bb0ff-e71f-4d37-97ce-2fb6a9cd1a4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revenue and receivables", "children": [{"id": "fa99cbbe-d2e2-42d6-a4f7-8f23d12483c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue recognition and cutoff"}, {"id": "33c0d149-5111-41d1-ba47-2578f23a62af", "type": "concept", "title": "Accounts receivable confirmations"}, {"id": "966c9755-82a7-4fd6-9e97-3bb5a2821158", "type": "concept", "title": "Allowance for credit losses"}], "description": "Revenue is often high risk because it drives performance and valuation."}, {"id": "4ce8e45e-2223-40df-be3b-f1a2048d735f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purchasing, inventory, and payroll", "children": [{"id": "6868d50f-bd46-473b-8adf-de27236d0627", "type": "concept", "title": "Three-way match and payables"}, {"id": "0320dbde-b830-4a3a-82ea-c1c5f805ef29", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory observation and costing"}, {"id": "ed985519-9e9f-48e7-b354-c836b41d6119", "type": "concept", "title": "Payroll authorization and accuracy"}], "description": "Students learn how operational cycles create financial reporting risks."}, {"id": "73c7ce06-e2fd-4175-8de5-115ebd3a2819", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cash, financing, and reporting", "children": [{"id": "f21ad811-57a7-4c9c-8a3d-9d7a014a4b4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Bank confirmations and reconciliations"}, {"id": "7d19e639-15cb-4e9e-8c1f-464a2357f7b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt covenants and equity transactions"}, {"id": "4ad473f6-7e33-401f-830b-a69729300d87", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial statement close and disclosure controls"}], "description": "Cycle work culminates in cash, debt, equity, estimates, and disclosures."}]}, {"id": "e7faf351-b969-4e65-9855-3359b1d67975", "type": "topic", "title": "Fraud Risk, Forensic Mindset, and Professional Skepticism", "description": "This module teaches students to identify fraud risk, evaluate red flags, and respond with appropriate audit and forensic procedures.", "children": [{"id": "79b0f3bf-653f-4f43-aeb3-c85073ab105a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fraud theory", "children": [{"id": "56536074-048b-4df4-94e2-9d7641a60c20", "type": "concept", "title": "Fraud triangle and fraud diamond"}, {"id": "3002347c-dd8a-4f9e-a4e4-9ecfa140cfd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset misappropriation, corruption, and financial statement fraud"}, {"id": "1b787a8a-b2bb-40d2-a3ba-8aa4a5579cbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Pressure, opportunity, rationalization, and capability"}], "description": "Students learn the behavioral and control conditions that make fraud possible."}, {"id": "ce732653-5d25-46a6-a53d-a86a1e185293", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fraud risk procedures", "children": [{"id": "cc0e5168-229f-494d-9f9b-e84240741a82", "type": "concept", "title": "Management inquiry and fraud brainstorming"}, {"id": "fc4ff78f-7158-4b1e-bafb-19ca59477da9", "type": "concept", "title": "Journal entry testing"}, {"id": "7c13289e-95a0-4aa5-97f4-557514092c11", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue fraud and management override"}], "description": "Audit standards require specific fraud brainstorming and response procedures."}, {"id": "38ba98d9-f4e7-4a86-a0c5-2fe0463a0223", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forensic mindset", "children": [{"id": "1d979cfc-0d69-4052-a2bd-2526f80d7764", "type": "concept", "title": "Red flags and anomaly patterns"}, {"id": "e9e88c72-3a4e-4f75-8188-cd0d796b6862", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence preservation and chain of custody"}, {"id": "294ccb9f-06bb-413f-8f46-8032a8754091", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviewing and escalation"}], "description": "A forensic lens sharpens skepticism without turning every audit into an investigation."}]}, {"id": "6fab2359-95cc-4d66-9c72-9cdb09386b59", "type": "topic", "title": "Audit Data Analytics, Continuous Auditing, and Visualization", "description": "Students learn modern audit analytics, population testing, exception analysis, process mining, and dashboard communication.", "children": [{"id": "3c2dc082-eacc-4b2b-945a-5a42d7b66a93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit data acquisition", "children": [{"id": "381e5d83-f067-4368-83c5-4f05c03c91b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Data requests and extraction"}, {"id": "3e042e76-6aa0-4145-b9f5-ff098ca7cec3", "type": "concept", "title": "Data-quality checks and reconciliations"}, {"id": "4580ebf8-fdab-4abc-b1ce-39ca97ef2a44", "type": "concept", "title": "Access controls and data lineage"}], "description": "Analytics begin with complete, accurate, and usable data."}, {"id": "14491ee4-b48a-465c-8c85-78eea0ecd612", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytic procedures", "children": [{"id": "c6948133-bb2f-4fbc-9556-70ac6d83ff77", "type": "concept", "title": "Journal entry analytics"}, {"id": "d32dc4d0-b8d5-48b8-a311-cb791848e792", "type": "concept", "title": "Benford analysis and anomaly detection"}, {"id": "6eaec86c-4bf4-476e-83e6-1debd6f6b115", "type": "concept", "title": "Process mining and transaction-flow analysis"}], "description": "Students learn methods that can test full populations and reveal hidden patterns."}, {"id": "82149b71-5eb9-47ea-9dc7-686d9e1c63dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visualization and communication", "children": [{"id": "d104301a-ff07-4853-a236-8192f91b702d", "type": "concept", "title": "Exception dashboards"}, {"id": "e6925f14-5720-4e5d-89f6-d92079c0f228", "type": "concept", "title": "Drill-down views"}, {"id": "f3f644e7-6bdb-4ca9-9941-0b894ebdcf86", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation of analytics-based evidence"}], "description": "Dashboards make exceptions, trends, and audit evidence more understandable."}]}, {"id": "430f1e09-e652-42d3-8fa0-f4be44713d75", "type": "topic", "title": "IT Audit, Cybersecurity Controls, SOC Reports, and Service Organizations", "description": "This topic builds competence in IT general controls, application controls, cybersecurity risk, and third-party assurance.", "children": [{"id": "e7a83a8d-187c-4e75-9db9-088e08fa507d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IT general controls", "children": [{"id": "75e54ec7-21c2-41c6-a6e5-36cbe1991833", "type": "concept", "title": "Access management"}, {"id": "a2d3ed0f-69ac-4274-a74c-22ecab3f008c", "type": "concept", "title": "Change management"}, {"id": "26d84c7f-dbb9-42d1-98fe-ae579883287a", "type": "concept", "title": "Backup, recovery, and operations controls"}], "description": "Reliable systems depend on controlled access, change, and operations."}, {"id": "1c6bc191-1cb5-4170-a332-00ae9bb98582", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Application and automated controls", "children": [{"id": "c3cc592b-fa46-4f29-a27d-b7e878bcc46a", "type": "concept", "title": "Input, processing, output, and interface controls"}, {"id": "0b1e7887-617c-4340-9fc4-66c4ec0b480f", "type": "concept", "title": "Configuration controls"}, {"id": "ba11c34c-0ea0-4ff5-8a8c-6252285c38f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Automated control testing"}], "description": "Many financial controls are embedded in systems rather than performed manually."}, {"id": "ab7bc56b-df40-42f8-bb02-c6e7cdb51ecc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Third-party and cyber assurance", "children": [{"id": "63d6db8a-0455-43a6-b4be-2126213feb0f", "type": "concept", "title": "SOC 1, SOC 2, and bridge letters"}, {"id": "be4b254f-88ae-4d97-9d26-114e21cb1eea", "type": "concept", "title": "Service organization controls"}, {"id": "45c2c6a0-331a-4a36-90c5-7f7c5409d148", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity incidents and audit response"}], "description": "Modern audits must evaluate outsourced systems and cybersecurity implications."}]}, {"id": "c3f6ebba-542c-4775-893f-15e83425ab8c", "type": "topic", "title": "Completing the Audit, Review, Quality Management, and Audit Reports", "description": "Students learn completion procedures, subsequent events, going concern, review, consultation, quality control, and report modifications.", "children": [{"id": "bc7ecb59-0799-46ab-beed-945ecb6cc356", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Completion procedures", "children": [{"id": "5eac2e7c-f73c-4162-84d6-f291fb87b0a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Subsequent events"}, {"id": "62c7a097-aaf1-4b00-a4a2-4510811c4e3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Going concern"}, {"id": "cfbb7fb9-f2fd-473f-ad5e-44574dbe479e", "type": "concept", "title": "Management representation letters"}], "description": "The final phase ensures evidence supports the opinion before the report is issued."}, {"id": "422e1185-47fb-453d-b77b-4b1e7cefae31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation and review", "children": [{"id": "8f8c487a-0959-4aa0-84ea-97f623a433ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Summary of uncorrected misstatements"}, {"id": "b4d5692c-4766-4d34-a1d9-a350f81f0982", "type": "concept", "title": "Review of disclosures"}, {"id": "1076883d-5f5a-4cab-92ce-6ed5f7ceda4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Engagement quality review"}], "description": "Auditors aggregate results and decide whether issues are material."}, {"id": "ebcbb5c2-428d-47fe-aa13-d1261acbd2b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit reporting", "children": [{"id": "c9a6378e-02e2-4701-9948-82414a0f9178", "type": "concept", "title": "Unmodified and modified opinions"}, {"id": "f5bbe521-0fe0-4b26-a180-defb6056a098", "type": "concept", "title": "Emphasis-of-matter and other-matter paragraphs"}, {"id": "e1253882-552a-4f76-aa75-1b989905ee21", "type": "concept", "title": "Critical audit matters and key audit matters"}], "description": "Students learn how conclusions become public or client-facing reports."}]}, {"id": "7152ccbe-1bd3-4f42-b3d3-5fbe4b95f0b4", "type": "topic", "title": "Other Assurance Services, ESG Assurance, and Emerging Audit Frontiers", "description": "This module extends auditing into 